SUSPECTED BUG: path only. The last hop reads "in checkExplicit, call to (validate.Name).Validate" at the span of the
Check[Name] call: the hops "in validate.Check[validate.Name], call to (Name).Validate" and "in checkExplicit, call to
validate.Check[validate.Name]" are collapsed into one that names the wrong callee. A non-generic forwarder keeps both hops.
The Error Set itself is as expected. Likely cause: the path builder folds hops through "synthetic" callees (meant
for bound-method and pointer-receiver wrappers), and generic instances are synthetic functions too.
Call site of the explicit instance Check[validate.Name]: must narrow to Name.Validate.
Expect ErrEmpty and concrete *TypedErr[string]; ErrNegative must not appear.
